class.description:
[AudioBusSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"audio_buses"[/code]: it stores the volume, mute and solo values of the buses of [AudioServer] for the player, loads them when the game starts and applies them before the first sound plays (in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SERVERS], right after the default bus layout is loaded and before the [SceneTree] exists, so no [AudioStreamPlayer] can start earlier).
The settings resource is an [AudioBusListSettings] with one [AudioBusSettings] entry per bus. Buses are identified by their name ([member AudioBusSettings.bus_name]), not by their index, so a game update that adds or reorders buses keeps the stored values. The defaults are the values of the bus layout when the game starts. Buses of the layout that have no stored entry yet (added by a game update) keep their layout values and are added to the list after loading. Stored buses that the layout does not have are skipped with a warning, or created if [member create_missing_buses] is [code]true[/code].
The file is [code]user://settings/audio_buses.ini[/code] by default. Because the settings resource holds nothing but the list, it can also be stored as CSV with one row per bus ([member ProjectSettings.settings/storage/format] set to [constant ResourceTextSerializer.FORMAT_CSV]). The output and input device are a separate domain, see [AudioDeviceSettingsServer].
All typed methods below go through [method ListSettingsServer.set_entry_value] or [method ListSettingsServer.add_entry]: in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_IMMEDIATE] a change is applied to [AudioServer] at once and saved at the end of the frame; in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_MANUAL] it waits for [method SettingsServer.apply].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# A volume slider from 0 to 100 %.
func _on_music_slider_value_changed(value):
	AudioBusSettingsServer.set_bus_volume_linear(&"Music", value / 100.0)

func _ready():
	$MusicSlider.value = AudioBusSettingsServer.get_bus_volume_linear(&"Music") * 100.0
	$MuteCheck.button_pressed = AudioBusSettingsServer.is_bus_mute(&"Master")

# A menu with "Apply" and "Cancel".
func open_menu():
	AudioBusSettingsServer.apply_mode = SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_MANUAL

func _on_apply_pressed():
	AudioBusSettingsServer.apply()

func _on_cancel_pressed():
	AudioBusSettingsServer.revert()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
// A volume slider from 0 to 100 %.
private void OnMusicSliderValueChanged(double value)
{
    AudioBusSettingsServer.SetBusVolumeLinear("Music", (float)(value / 100.0));
}

public override void _Ready()
{
    GetNode<Slider>("MusicSlider").Value = AudioBusSettingsServer.GetBusVolumeLinear("Music") * 100.0;
    GetNode<CheckBox>("MuteCheck").ButtonPressed = AudioBusSettingsServer.IsBusMute("Master");
}

// A menu with "Apply" and "Cancel". Methods of the base classes are called through Singleton.
private void OpenMenu()
{
    AudioBusSettingsServer.Singleton.ApplyMode = SettingsServer.ApplyModeEnum.Manual;
}

private void OnApplyPressed()
{
    AudioBusSettingsServer.Singleton.Apply();
}

private void OnCancelPressed()
{
    AudioBusSettingsServer.Singleton.Revert();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] In C#, the static class [code skip-lint]AudioBusSettingsServer[/code] only has the methods of this class. The methods of [SettingsServer] and [ListSettingsServer] are called through [code]AudioBusSettingsServer.Singleton[/code].
[b]Note:[/b] [method AudioServer.set_bus_layout] replaces all bus values. If the game switches the bus layout at runtime, the stored values are not applied to the new layout automatically.
